            <ArticleTitle>Respiratory care of older adults after cardiac surgery.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>71-83</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Older adults are at risk for pulmonary complications and prolonged mechanical ventilation after cardiac surgery. A patient-centered conceptualization of ventilatory support provides a framework for preoperative assessment of postoperative management of older adults at risk for postoperative pulmonary complications. Ventilatory support is a dynamic process whereby physiologic, pathophysiologic, and psychosocial patient variables influence and interact with postoperative clinical practice variables. Research-based respiratory care interventions are proposed to improve recovery outcomes in older adults after cardiac surgery.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
